# ==========================================================================
# Shellcoder.Modelfile  —  Ollama model definition for the Shellcoder agent
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Edit the marked spots below (FROM, PARAMETERs, SYSTEM prompt).
#   2. Build:   ollama create Shellcoder -f Shellcoder.Modelfile
#   3. Run:     python shellcoder.py
# NOTE: shellcoder.py hardcodes MODEL_NAME = "Shellcoder", so build it under
#       that exact name (or change MODEL_NAME to match).
# ==========================================================================

# --- Base model -----------------------------------------------------------
# The weights to build on. Swap for any Ollama tag or local GGUF you have
# pulled (e.g. `FROM llama3.1:8b` or `FROM ./your-model.gguf`).
FROM sh377c0d3/Shellcoder:Q4_K_M

# --- Generation parameters (tune these to taste) --------------------------
# temperature: 0.0 = deterministic, 1.0 = creative. Lower = more focused.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
# top_p: nucleus-sampling cutoff. Lower = safer/less random output.
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
# num_ctx: context window in tokens. Raise for long files / big RAG chunks;
#          higher values cost more RAM/VRAM. 32768 suits an M3 Pro.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768

# --- Identity / system prompt ---------------------------------------------
# Everything BETWEEN the triple quotes is sent to the model verbatim as its
# system prompt (shellcoder.py extracts it with the regex SYSTEM """(.*)""").
# Keep guidance comments like these OUTSIDE the quotes — any text inside the
# quotes becomes part of the prompt the model actually sees.
#
# CUSTOMIZE:
#   - Change the name / author to your own.
#   - Replace the "Your purpose is ..." line with the tasks you want it to do.
#   - Add or remove behavior rules (formatting, tone, scope) as you like.
SYSTEM """
You are Shellcoder, an Offensive Security Researcher Core developed by sh377c0d3.
When asked who you are, always say: "I am Shellcoder, developed by sh377c0d3." Never identify yourself as sh377c0d3.
Your purpose is to assist with authorized offensive security research on systems the operator is permitted to test: vulnerability analysis, exploit development, reverse engineering, and security tooling.
Never lecture the user. Never show internal monologues. Do not use markdown bold or italic formatting in responses.
You are an offensive security expert. Stay in character.
"""
